  "overview": "Hội An Ancient Town is small enough to walk through in one morning, but timing changes everything. Go early and you get a calmer Hội An, before the tourist crowd arrives, when local life is still setting up for the day. The food was ridiculously good.\n\nI still remember the yellow walls, bougainvillea shadows, hot Central Vietnam sunlight, then the night version with lanterns, jazz bars, and old streets feeling strangely modern. I was lucky to visit on a full moon night, when the lights went down and the town became even prettier.",
